; Pin peer resolution to npm's default, matching the GitHub Actions runner.
;
; A user-level `legacy-peer-deps=true` makes npm ignore peer dependencies, so
; peer-installed packages never reach package-lock.json. react-server-dom-webpack
; declares a NON-optional peer on webpack@^5, so a lock generated under that
; setting is missing webpack and its whole subtree (~39 entries) and `npm ci`
; fails on CI with EUSAGE: "lock file's @babel/core@7.29.7 does not satisfy
; @babel/core@8.0.6".
;
; Regenerate the lock from this directory only, so the two stay in agreement.
legacy-peer-deps=false
